course: dictionary
lesson: 3488
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The dictionary gives fancy at least four, so you must check the sentence to find the right one. «The cake was fancy, with gold stars on top.» Here fancy means decorated and special, not plain.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Do you fancy a biscuit?» In this sentence, fancy means want. Try the meaning in the sentence: "Do you want a biscuit?" It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Some phrases use fancy in a special way. «Take a fancy to» means start to like, so «Sam took a fancy to the puppy» means Sam started to like it. «Fancy that!» is a way of saying how surprising, and the words around it show you the surprise.
fact: Fancy can mean decorated, special or expensive, not plain.
fact: In British, Australian and Irish English, to fancy something means to want it or like the idea of it.
fact: «Take a fancy to» means start to like.
fact: «Fancy that!» means how surprising.
fact: «Nothing fancy» means simple, with no extras.
exercise: «The cake was fancy, with gold stars on top.» What does fancy mean here? | Cheap and old | Cold and wet | Burnt | * Decorated and special, not plain
exercise: Ella asks, «Do you fancy a biscuit?» What is she asking? | Whether you dropped a biscuit | * Whether you want a biscuit | Whether you can count the biscuits
exercise: Sam says he has taken a fancy to the new puppy. What does «take a fancy to» mean? | * Start to like | Start to forget | Start to sell | Start to run away from
test:
Maya says «Fancy that!» when she hears the news. What does she mean? | Let's go to bed | * How surprising | How sleepy she is | How cheap it was
Which sentence uses fancy to mean decorated or special? | We ate plain toast for lunch | * We ate fancy cakes at the party | We walked fast to school | We put the bags on the floor
exam:
Which meaning fits «Do you fancy a walk?» | Can you walk very fast? | Did you walk yesterday? | * Do you want to go for a walk? | Are you too tired to walk?
